questions.question_text:
A ball's height is $h=-5t^2+10t$ metres after $t$ seconds. Use the graph to find its maximum height and when it occurs.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=3,ymin=0,ymax=7,xtick={0,0.5,...,3},ytick={0,1,...,7},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (s)},ylabel={$h$ (m)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:2,samples=100] {-5*x*x+10*x};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rocket's height is $h=-5t^2+50t$ metres after $t$ seconds. Use the graph to find when it returns to the ground.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=11,ymin=0,ymax=140,xtick={0,1,...,11},ytick={0,20,...,140},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (s)},ylabel={$h$ (m)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:10,samples=100] {-5*x*x+50*x};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ball is thrown from a ledge, so its height is $h=-5t^2+15t+2$ metres after $t$ seconds. Use the graph to state the height from which it is thrown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=4,ymin=0,ymax=16,xtick={0,0.5,...,4},ytick={0,2,...,16},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (s)},ylabel={$h$ (m)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:3.13,samples=100] {-5*x*x+15*x+2};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ball's height is $h=-5t^2+30t$ metres after $t$ seconds. Use the graph to find the two times when the ball is $40$ m high.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=7,ymin=0,ymax=50,xtick={0,1,...,7},ytick={0,10,...,50},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (s)},ylabel={$h$ (m)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:6,samples=100] {-5*x*x+30*x};
\addplot[dashed,gray,domain=0:6] {40};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A stall's revenue is the curve $R=-x^2+6x$ and its cost is the line $C=5$, both in hundreds of dollars, where $x$ is the number of boxes sold. Use the graph to find the break-even points.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=7,ymin=0,ymax=11,xtick={0,1,...,7},ytick={0,1,...,11},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$\$ (100s)$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:6,samples=100] {-x*x+6*x};
\addplot[thick,red!75!black,dashed,domain=0:7] {5};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The income and cost graphs for a coffee cart are drawn on the same axes and cross at $(4,80)$, where $x$ is the number of drinks (in tens) and the amount is in dollars. What does this crossing point tell you?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=9,ymin=0,ymax=130,xtick={0,1,...,9},ytick={0,20,...,120},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$\$$}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:8.5,samples=100] {-2*x*x+28*x};
\addplot[thick,red!75!black,dashed,domain=0:9] {12*x+32};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A shop raises its prices. Its income for a price rise of $\$x$ is $I=-10x^2+80x+1200$. Use the graph to find the price rise that gives the maximum income.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=9,ymin=0,ymax=1500,xtick={0,1,...,9},ytick={0,200,...,1400},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$ (\$)},ylabel={$I$ (\$)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:9,samples=100] {-10*x*x+80*x+1200};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ball's height is $h=-5t^2+40t$ metres after $t$ seconds. Use the graph to find the total time for which the ball is above $75$ m.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=6.5cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=8,ymin=0,ymax=90,xtick={0,1,...,8},ytick={0,20,...,80},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (s)},ylabel={$h$ (m)}]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:8,samples=100] {-5*x*x+40*x};
\addplot[dashed,gray,domain=0:8] {75};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
